91. (22) When a man is happy and content in placing wrong view foremost of the sort beginning "There is no danger in sense desires"
(M I 307), and either enjoys sense desires with consciousness that in its own individual essence is eager without being urged,
or believes auspicious sights, etc., have a real substantial core, then the first kind of unprofitable consciousness arises (23);
